.TH DNSNAME 1 "2026-05-23" "hako" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dnsname \- reverse DNS lookup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dnsname
.RI [ @nameserver ]
.I ip
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dnsname
sends a PTR query for the given IPv4 address and prints the resulting
hostnames, one per line.
The address is automatically converted to the standard
.I d.c.b.a.in-addr.arpa
form before querying.
.PP
If no PTR records are returned, a message is printed to stdout and the
command exits successfully.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI @ nameserver
Use the specified IPv4 nameserver instead of the default (8.8.8.8).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Reverse-look up an address:
.B dnsname 8.8.8.8
.TP
Use a custom nameserver:
.B dnsname @1.1.1.1 8.8.4.4
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success (including the case where no PTR records exist).
.TP
1
Invalid argument or DNS error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dig (1)
